From 73b30bb6f1ba34094285e1df83ad91d3c7ffcc85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:33:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 41/48] policy: relay OP_CHECKMLDSA44 spends only once active,
 and in two templates

- SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_MLDSA44 joins the mandatory, and so the standard,
  script verification flags, but the mempool leaves it out while the
  next block is below the activation height. There the byte is still an
  OP_SUCCESSx, and DISCOURAGE_OP_SUCCESS keeps every spend that executes
  it out of the mempool, validly signed or not: an output that is not
  protected yet is not relayed as if it were.
- A reorganization that puts the next block back below the activation
  height removes the transactions that execute the opcode in a P2MR
  leaf, with their descendants. removeForReorg does not check scripts
  again, and a block below the activation height would otherwise include
  them without the check they were accepted under. A node with
  -acceptnonstdtxn=1 can hold spends of other scripts than the
  templates, so the test is any executed P2MR leaf whose opcodes include
  OP_CHECKMLDSA44.
- P2MR leaves keep the 80-byte limit on witness elements, except for the
  five signature chunks of two leaf templates, byte for byte:
  S1 <pk[0]> <pk[1]> <pk[2]> OP_CHECKMLDSA44, and
  S2 S1 OP_VERIFY <x-only key> OP_CHECKSIG.
  The chunks must have their exact sizes and the leaf must be at depth
  one or more. Other scripts that use the opcode are not standard.
---
